BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Pain And The Power (Advance Screening)
DTSTART:20260914T020000Z
DTEND:20260914T041500Z
DTSTAMP:20260914T020000Z
UID:JvC7kYEJg5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nPresented by Portugal. The Man 
 / KNIK / PortuGAYThe Pain and The Power is an unflinching documentary 
 portrait of artist\, activist\, and survivor Logan Lynn\, by filmmaker Cai
  Indermaur.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/the-pain-and-the-po
 wer-(advance-screening)\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Land of the Dead: it's for the gays
DTSTART:20261031T014500Z
DTEND:20261031T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T014500Z
UID:9Sifmjwjyg
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nPresented by Scorpio Rising Prod
 uctions. Land of the Dead: it’s for the gays is a dark\, campy horror c
 omedy that explores the intersections of gender identity\, addiction\, tra
 uma\, and Queerness. Through Mel’s confrontation with a literal demon fr
 om their past\, the film examines the ways unresolved pain can shape ident
 ity\, relationships\, and self-acceptance. Blending supernatural horror wi
 th Queer humor and emotional depth\, the story uses camp as a tool for bot
 h survival and reclamation\, creating a space where confronting the past b
 ecomes a path toward healing and embracing one’s authentic self.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/land-of-the-dead-its-for-the-gays\n\nE
 stimated start: 19:00
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
